# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# HobeRadius — Docker build context ALLOWLIST (deny-by-default).
#
# WHY: the image ballooned to ~10.7GB because the build context is the
# repo ROOT (deploy/docker-compose.yml: `context: ..`) and the Dockerfile
# used `COPY . /app` with a weak denylist. On the production server the
# repo dir accumulates untracked multi-GB junk that a denylist can never
# enumerate reliably: the live SQLite DB + WAL under instance/ (bind-
# mounted at runtime anyway), DB backup archives, customer migration
# dumps (*.sql / *.sql.gz / migration_samples/), logs, agent worktrees…
#
# STRATEGY: deny EVERYTHING (`*`), then re-include ONLY what the image
# needs. Anything new that appears on the server — whatever it is —
# stays out of the context by default. The runtime set is:
#   app/           code + templates + static + DB migrations
#   translations/  Flask-Babel catalogs (loaded from project root)
#   tools/         owner-run CLIs (docker exec hoberadius python tools/…)
#   deploy/        gunicorn.conf.py (CMD) + entrypoint.sh (ENTRYPOINT)
#   wsgi.py / requirements.txt / babel.cfg
#
# NOTE: instance/, logs/, backups/ are BIND MOUNTS in docker-compose —
# they must never be baked into the image (the Dockerfile mkdir -p's the
# mount points). app/static/uploads IS included when present: compose
# does not mount it, so baked files are the only way runtime uploads
# survive a rebuild (pre-existing behaviour, kept unchanged).
#
# The freeradius image has its own context (deploy/freeradius) and is
# NOT affected by this file.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── deny everything by default ──
*

# ── runtime allowlist ──
!app
!translations
!tools
!deploy
!wsgi.py
!requirements.txt
!babel.cfg

# ── re-deny generated/cache/secret junk inside the allowed dirs ──
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.DS_Store
# databases / dumps / archives can never enter the image, wherever they sit
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sql
# …EXCEPT the schema migrations — required at runtime (migrations_runner
# applies app/radius/db/migrations/*.sql on startup). Only that exact dir.
!app/radius/db/migrations/*.sql
**/*.sql.gz
**/*.gz
**/*.zip
**/*.tar
**/*.tgz
**/*.bak
**/*.old
**/*.tmp
**/*.log
# secrets — belt & braces (also gitignored; env comes via compose env_file)
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*firebase*adminsdk*.json
**/service-account*.json
**/google-credentials*.json
